# Project Ages: JourneyMap is the pack's map (M key), and it marks where you die.
# FTB Chunks (claims; its map is on Shift+M) makes no death waypoints of its own and draws no waypoints
# in the world. So every waypoint beam in the world is JourneyMap's, and JourneyMap's settings control them all.
# 0.7.2, Burrahndone's report: a death beam stayed after the death waypoint was deleted in JourneyMap
# (it was FTB Chunks' own death waypoint).
# FTB Chunks fills in its other settings itself when the game starts.

{
	waypoints: {
		# Create death waypoints on death (JourneyMap already does)
		death_waypoints: false

		# Show waypoints in world: beams and dots (FTB Chunks' map still shows its waypoints)
		in_world_waypoints: false
	}
}
